There is an even sharper warning. Add the same constant $C$ to every frequency: $\omega(k)\longrightarrow \omega(k)+C.$ The constant could, for example, represent a common rest-energy contribution such as $mc_{\mathrm{light}}^2$, but its particular name is unimportant. Here $C$ is an energy offset, not the speed of light. The phase velocity changes to $v_{\mathrm{phase}}\longrightarrow
\frac{\omega(k)+C}{k}
=v_{\mathrm{phase}}+\frac{C}{k}.$ Yet adding the same constant to every energy changes no energy difference and hence no nonrelativistic physics.

